# Schedules for the scheduler container (supercronic, standard cron syntax, UTC).
# Collectors are added here as they land; each one fetches any days it missed.

# Every hour: confirm the database and object storage are reachable.
0 * * * * dr check

# Every day at 04:30 UTC: SEAP direct purchases finalized up to yesterday.
30 4 * * * dr collect seap-direct

# Every day at 05:30 UTC: SEAP award notices published up to yesterday, with the
# contracts, winners, detail and versions of each (three requests or more per notice,
# a few minutes a day).
30 5 * * * dr collect seap-awards

# Every day at 07:30 UTC: the detail and versions of the notices that a failed request
# left without them (nothing to ask for on most days); then, once it ends, so that two
# jobs never ask SEAP at once, the lines and conditions of accepted direct purchases of
# 100,000 lei or more, newest first, one request each. At most 4,000 a run (about an
# hour and a half): the 30,000 held when this began are done in about eight days, then
# about a hundred new ones a day.
30 7 * * * dr collect seap-award-details; dr collect seap-direct-details --limit 4000

# Every day at 08:30 UTC, after the SEAP jobs: ANAF's record (county and locality) of the
# institutions and companies they brought that ANAF was not asked about yet, 100 tax IDs
# a call, then every entity placed again. A few calls on most days, none when nothing
# is new.
30 8 * * * dr collect anaf

# Every day at 09:00 UTC: the newest edition of the PNRR dashboard data (MIPE), if it is
# not loaded yet. One small request on most days; about 6.5 MB when an edition is new,
# every two weeks or so.
0 9 * * * dr collect pnrr

# On the 1st of every month at 09:30 UTC: the Anghel Saligny payment files and SEAP's
# contract exports (data.gov.ro) not held yet. The ministry adds a payment file about
# monthly and SEAP an export each quarter; a file already held is not downloaded again,
# so a month with nothing new costs a few calls. In this order: a new payment file can
# name builders, whose contracts the stored exports are read again for, then a new
# export keeps those of every builder known. Each step ties the payments again.
30 9 1 * * dr collect pnias-payments && dr reparse seap-exports && dr collect seap-exports
